{"posts":[{"id":"hs_p117_1451","t":"So important to know the difference between Supply/Demand, FL, Origins, and ORFL\n\nI am going to spend some time practicing this. Some of my posts last night are not correct.\n\nSalivan says \"S/D is a reaction to a FL\"\n\nHe also says:Origins are created after S/D is created\"\n\nS/D, Origins, ORFl's, etc... exist on all time frames, in each scale. Understanding how to draw them (and why they are important) is a key part of keeping scale straight.\n\nAnd here is the same drawing with more detail:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1451","p":117,"im":["88e96b8f31bfe0267ccbd7b6ccc8ddc3e4496cde","5cdaf438f077f9799803cc5a630ccbfd9ba5746b"],"m":1451},{"id":"hs_p117_1452","t":"Example of origin only (not ORFL)\n\nExample of ORFL being formed:\n\n** ORFL are important because they act as a magnet for price (targets). If you haven't read Salivan's post in my journal about magnetic attraction/repulsion (found in my journal on Post # 901), it is definitely worth reading. Of course, ORFL are only useful if you know how to draw them correctly I need to practice this until I am blue in the face. I think 75% of the battle is knowing how to draw these zones correctly, within each scale. The rest is just understanding how price moves from decision to decision or target to target.\n\nHere is a link to Post # 901:\n\nwww.readthemarket.com/index.php/en/forum...ng-journal?start=900","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1452","p":117,"im":["a1a11cdfb1b1af1cc580cffb6201ed12482513d2","c201ed14ae63cd983dacccf23196502fd9206c82"],"m":1452},{"id":"hs_p117_1453","t":"EUR-USD Practice:\n\nHere is a reaction...to a FL to the left. There is another demand that is formed as a result of a reaction to a FL even further left.\n\nQuestion: if Origins are formed as a result of reacting to S/D zone, what happens if price doesn't come back to react to the S/D zone? See chart below...does this mean there is no origin for this reaction?\n\nHere is the reaction (further to the left). In this case, demand zones is formed and price reacts to it. I think this is correct way to drawn ORFL Up in this scale. Some situations are clear and others are a bit confusing...","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1453","p":117,"im":["1f33f24a67e71cd0720f85184e1805bbaedb7e4c","00351b286c379845681dc16b10b34de8a138d485","325c0cab141fbf6d002dac88a69d0bb8edf56116","15bc5a64dcf2d700760e18f84f7265c6b8092399"],"m":1453},{"id":"hs_p117_1454","t":"Note to self:\n\nRegardless of how good the analysis is...don't take a trade a day before new years weekend! Not enough liquidity to feel safe setting stop loss.\n\nGot slipped over 60 pips....","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1454","p":117,"im":["9eeb24edfdaed60d129e02dece87549f8e79ca35"],"m":1454},{"id":"hs_p117_1455","t":"Back to practicing:\n\nUSD-CHF:\n\nI will focus on this reaction. Find Supply and ORFL - Down (in this scale)\n\nIs this the correct way:\n\nOr is this the correct way?","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1455","p":117,"im":["2cd1cab31618dad17f85e93041d264c02be22157","5790dbece45c97d8f6213437b2baf787abe0963c","3d9ad93c884a60854d74730850b1f5bc2c33baa3"],"m":1455},{"id":"hs_p117_1456","t":"USD-CHF:\n\nThis one looks right to me...\n\nAnother tough one.. not ORFL","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1456","p":117,"im":["55c54ce5486dd81f8083444578234d7def43177e","67b859054026b051308eee75485cc0597faef6d2"],"m":1456},{"id":"hs_p117_1457","t":"I want to correct a mistake I made on analyzing NZD-USD yesterday.\n\nThis is correct:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1457","p":117,"im":["5c672782ad24448e8b6c2cdf76a336a1f0b0da64"],"m":1457},{"id":"hs_p117_1458","t":"NZD-USD - Expanded Analysis:\n\nFocus on ORFL's and wait for them to be broken. The FL that forms after the break is an important zone. Every EG of important level begins a new FL Box.\n\nSame Analysis except on EUR-AUD:\n\nEUR-JPY: More of the same.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1458","p":117,"im":["573fbe5655fdf04d152ada27c0857e6007732f72","3c5279a8ccdba35401804bc777e6ae93ed606862","e12eb6f89a2029fbbb96f2491c368c324d2baf19"],"m":1458},{"id":"hs_p117_1459","t":"GBP-USD - More practice finding Origins/ORFL's/EG etc...\n\nLet's focus in on the Green rectangle that I drew in the chart above:\n\nFind the Origin up for the green rectangle's scale. Watch how price reacts to this FL Box. See how nicely price bounces at the ORFL - UP?\n\nMore of the same- Another ORFL - UP is formed and price bounces @ MPL","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1459","p":117,"im":["5176936e146ad3c4bb9654eddb9a7f30bf0442d3","6851c0e1c616a6629649c4b44f9568ec45226032","5a75f54cf18a78dead238e0b38b76b73ac561992"],"m":1459},{"id":"hs_p117_1460","t":"GBP-USD\n\nThis is a chart (recreated) that Salivan posted on Persian RTM. He shows the MPL as being the blue dotted line. The Green rectangle is the FL. I can't seem to figure this out...I see people posting MPL's like this with regularity on RTM but I am confused. Why isn't the MPL the upper green line (extreme zone of the FL)?\n\nAnyone know why the MPL is sometimes shown this way, and other times shown as the extreme edge of the FL Box?\n\n1-Min close-up:\n\n15-Min Chart\n\nHere is salivan's Chart:\n\nFound: www.readthemarket.com/index.php/en/forum/165/2721-salivan","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1460","p":117,"im":["4fb2ba65c88244341c8ec35176d919424ce59371","e6006dc37e362211b9c2a6d0cbcb6ad4dd919ec3","4885c1105cefabf54158f8d9287cbf0b5db42caf","4470bdea8b3ffeed6c286534cd4ceece21d283c4"],"m":1460},{"id":"hs_p117_1461","t":"EUR-GBP:\n\nI have a hard time identifying the Origin when price does this:\n\nHere is a diagram that explains my problem: When price makes the highest high in the reaction, and price reacts to this HH, the OR is easier to find.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1461","p":117,"im":["1c67c5e59292b5fe8676330e78e97c81ab5f5b3b","8809c022dc39f35d74234138fb760cf24750daa3"],"m":1461},{"id":"hs_p117_1462","t":"EUR-GBP:\n\nChart # 1: Basic, showing major FL Boxes in one scale\n\nI will focus in on the green rectangle for the next chart:\n\nAnd within the Green FL Box there is a swing high and a swing low. Price falls from the swing high, and it rises from the swing low.\n\nNot sure if this is right, but here is the origin up and down in this scale.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1462","p":117,"im":["261dd23cea9e9f932b1839a90d8d2bcb5147bbbc","cef3189ea4ade8f37015db1b3ca8442bf9fc2e42","7dd6cab03e60b8c7b59ffe0d8b7f74952cb7bfc6"],"m":1462},{"id":"hs_p117_1463","t":"EUR-GBP: Continued....\n\nBlue FL Box Details: Focusing on Origin Down and price's reaction to it.\n\nClose up 1-min chart:\n\nBlack dotted line shows where price bounces the first time.\n\nHTF View of the bounce:\n\nThe reaction denoted by the black arrow above (where price bounced) is itself a reaction. In a new scale, a new ORFL down is created (price is reacting to FL creating supply). All this is happening within different scales... just like a Russian nested doll.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1463","p":117,"im":["441c1c8bba63f175267a5272b40da4d6f97fb746","6db4fd58e51fa56f0ac44d54cb172e1e074d1b9d","056b08b4b50023e3aa1482d9ab2bf12dc2836967","ad8290a7f267486f7bd205fec32131a0a9cd2100","e21d2c8f0bbefee41286f9a1bf2a757a1eee47ba"],"m":1463},{"id":"hs_p117_1464","t":"EUR-GBP - New Example on 4-HR Chart:\n\nCan't See Origin Down clearly in HTF, so I will drop down to LTF for more PA detail.\n\nHere is a bigger picture view: As you can see, there are many scales within this scale.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1464","p":117,"im":["f53cce0e4fedb882a9327ba6b776aa7e1cc10cd8","65298289bf1fb0dd47043404a4e8f56386e96a59","fc36ac075a87cb60209460c7e5e13e1b0e2bf535"],"m":1464},{"id":"hs_p117_1465","t":"EUR-GBP - More of the same analysis. Just looking in the past.\n\n4-Hour chart back in 2012: We see the same patterns unfolding... over and over again.\n\nThe ORFL is hard to see in this scale...need to drop down to LTF.\n\nNow look for ORFL - UP - In this scale...\n\nNotice how every reaction to a FL creates a new supply/demand zone & Origin up/down... Look at the grey rectangle that shows ORFL - Down. When price comes back to test this zone, it reacts and creates supply. After the supply is created, there is an ORFL that forms (it forms on reaction to the newly created supply).\n\n...And a new zone is born when price engulfs ORFL UP...look at the green rectangle to the very right of the chart.\n\nLet's look closer at this new FL Box (shaded green)","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1465","p":117,"im":["8423b38a324860d1803204391bafb18a98e37b85","3470c8c5a2202e27ae0c04db68df26f41c70ae9b","e8d235f1c6d4ff91d90e5882ebb1181b9ea903d4","1c322f891a61944644b81f482e799980ae7beb41","f79833fb496186566fb5a3fe354a1e97c0f87417"],"m":1465},{"id":"hs_p117_1466","t":"Continued from post above (EUR-GBP)\n\nHere is ORFL UP and ORFL Down within this FL Box's scale:\n\nZoom out to see more detail...price engulfs this ORFL Down.\n\nSee how price bounces at first test of TG for Longs/ORFL Down.\n\nAfter EG, I look higher for scale ORFL Down. I see two levels (I drew them back in post # 1463)\n\nSee how price bounces at first..test. Price comes back to hit MPL. Both reactions provide nice bounce.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1466","p":117,"im":["93f226a89337c03cfaab28b73480a086d3fb7779","2b9c434c4171df781bb0bf7a4ef5bbe29a34aabc","0509f656b5501b58be7bf36a209b58642af59f3d"],"m":1466},{"id":"hs_p117_1467","t":"hoeschec wrote: So important to know the difference between Supply/Demand, FL, Origins, and ORFL\n\nI am going to spend some time practicing this. Some of my posts last night are not correct.\n\nSalivan says \"S/D is a reaction to a FL\"\n\nHe also says:Origins are created after S/D is created\"\n\nS/D, Origins, ORFl's, etc... exist on all time frames, in each scale. Understanding how to draw them (and why they are important) is a key part of keeping scale straight.\n\nHi H your hard-work really inspiration for other trader who want to learn trading... & i m sure you are going to be a great trader very soon.. i have attached two pic for you hope you will find something interesting there (one from Master Salivan & one from Master Les_Paul (sorry for my poor English)","a":"Nbr42","d":"","n":"#1467","p":117,"im":["88e96b8f31bfe0267ccbd7b6ccc8ddc3e4496cde","5cdaf438f077f9799803cc5a630ccbfd9ba5746b","f8914812c9e7f73f16da10358536aaf378ef5db7","3319f87945c0d99d927df66a723c88d5b6916f15"],"m":1467},{"id":"hs_p117_1468","t":"Nbr42 wrote:\n\nhoeschec wrote: So important to know the difference between Supply/Demand, FL, Origins, and ORFL\n\nI am going to spend some time practicing this. Some of my posts last night are not correct.\n\nSalivan says \"S/D is a reaction to a FL\"\n\nHe also says:Origins are created after S/D is created\"\n\nS/D, Origins, ORFl's, etc... exist on all time frames, in each scale. Understanding how to draw them (and why they are important) is a key part of keeping scale straight.\n\nHey NBR42 - Thanks for the reminder of LP's sweet FTR\n\nLooks like his sweet FTR is the same as trading the FTB to the Origin that forms after supply/demand reaction.\n\nThe FTB + reaction to the Origin that forms after SD reaction to higher TF FL turns the Origin in to a ORFL.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1468","p":117,"im":["88e96b8f31bfe0267ccbd7b6ccc8ddc3e4496cde","5cdaf438f077f9799803cc5a630ccbfd9ba5746b","f8914812c9e7f73f16da10358536aaf378ef5db7","3319f87945c0d99d927df66a723c88d5b6916f15"],"m":1468},{"id":"hs_p117_1469","t":"AUD- JPY:\n\nAnother example A/J\n\nPrice just seems to bounce from ORFL to ORFL\n\nHere is detail showing the zone price is reacting to:\n\nThis shows EG of a ORFL - UP. New FL Box is formed as a result and within this scale there is another Origin down.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1469","p":117,"im":["5b67246a8e7786d1b84d68d800bc2612ae25dfbe","cbb1e8d368cb527973093d164b26a1662c68f75c","9d43e2cdbfd4da8e6699588b47835540892e2f51","eafe869659312d2a9e62c50d0a20e270cdcd5647"],"m":1469},{"id":"hs_p117_1470","t":"AUD-JPY:\n\nLook at the reaction here...1:20 RR on this trade.\n\nFL Boxes drawn within FL Boxes....using price's reaction to ORFL as a compass for future price intentions.\n\nHTF View: Once I fully understand how to draw these levels I will focus on price's interaction (EG/FO) to them. This is when scale really comes in. Targets met vs unmet etc...","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1470","p":117,"im":["917c496ae2bbd306c8752dd011c3d2f6274bd6e0","1e781245cb878ab9238c8e39f5b8d2a93b5f9c9c","57cd330dff2d647c9fed77745c0618034c1dd11e"],"m":1470},{"id":"hs_p117_1471","t":"HTF Analysis of EUR-NZD:\n\nLook how price reacts perfectly to the MPL (QM).\n\nPrice tested and created supply on first reaction, then came back to MPL.\n\nCreation of supply on 1st reaction is a perfect trap to set for the future FO to MPL.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1471","p":117,"im":["9c8b49efcb18e80eb4fa3c9ad871f1f34f81b83d"],"m":1471},{"id":"hs_p117_1472","t":"EUR-NZD\n\nThis chart shows EG Vs. FO.","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1472","p":117,"im":["76f4b6a2e64d2fda4552a23b80c6096a6725ee3c"],"m":1472},{"id":"hs_p117_1473","t":"Happy New Year Everyone!\n\nI am looking forward to a new year of trading.\n\nThe more I learn, the more excited I am for what lies ahead.\n\nThe good news: as hard as these concepts are to understand and implement, the market tends to repeat the same thing over and over again in each scale. So....once you understand it is just the same analysis over and over again\n\nI will keep practicing and this will be a fantastic year!","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1473","p":117,"im":[],"m":1473},{"id":"hs_p117_1474","t":"EUR-GBP:\n\nMore Detail...it gets more confusing with scale.\n\nClose up of red rectangle:","a":"hoeschec","d":"","n":"#1474","p":117,"im":["971f9906ac9559138761584b26bcf6af8891f96f","6384fdd8136e8074ba87bb70ba96f33e4a863c26","712e8e22d9f17cd90211ea1d6d607037b2007d1e","5963cfc021ec4e4d04bd58f0e9105fd98f776dbc","29679c6375ba26e6a80ec21f3595f3c61b8538a1"],"m":1474},{"id":"hs_p117_1475","t":"EUR-GBP:\n\nClose up of the green FL Box from the example in the post 